  "description": "An Aziel Eliab Project: independent historical newspaper and five-volume archive examining the death of U.S. Representative Marion Zioncheck in Seattle on 7 August 1936. The official report called it suicide from a fifth-floor Arctic Building office. This project publishes the record for re-reading. It does not invent court holdings, FOIA denial letters, or quotes beyond what the volumes and cited papers print.",
